    "C01","C03","C13","C15","C19","C24","C08","C09","C14",
    "C25","C31","C36","C33","C37","C38"
  ],
  "claims": [
    {
      "claim": "The query is a permanently charged quaternary ammonium morphinan with a phenolic OH and ketone; the permanent positive charge is a major barrier to passive oral absorption, and the low-F phenolic/first-pass-liable contexts are the most relevant transfer templates.",
      "card_ids": ["C04","C07","C16","C20","C23","C33","C37"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Multiple transferable human low-F contexts report absolute oral bioavailability below 20%: UK-224,671 3.6% fed and 7.5% fasted; estradiol 4-11%; MK-458 ~4-5%; rotigotine low/essentially none; catechins ~1.7% or modeled F 0.01-0.1.",
      "card_ids": ["C12","C17","C04","C07","C16","C20","C02","C11","C21","C22","C23","C01","C03","C13","C15","C19","C24","C08","C09","C14"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L2 records reinforce the low-F direction: UK-224,671 remained 3.6% fed; estradiol oral bioavailability is ~10% and 1-12%; rotigotine has poor/essentially no oral bioavailability; PHNO is low.",
      "card_ids": ["C25","C31","C36","C33","C37","C38"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L3 oral AUC/Cmax records for oxycodone, oxymorphone, and ethinyl estradiol report relative formulation ratios, tmax, or steroid exposure without matched IV absolute F for the query; they do not provide affirmative threshold-relevant evidence for the query.",
      "card_ids": ["C41","C42","C43","C44","C45","C46","C47","C48","C49","C50","C51","C52"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "The only high-F context, pethidine (F 0.48-0.57, ~50%), is not transferable because it is a small lipophilic tertiary amine ester lacking the quaternary ammonium charge and phenolic first-pass liabilities; rat EC values of 31-39% are species/formulation-specific and not applicable.",
      "card_ids": ["C05","C06","C10","C18","C30","C26","C29"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "oral_auc_cmax_exposure",
      "applicability": "low",
      "direction": "neutral_or_unclear",
      "decision_effect": "no_change",
      "card_ids": ["C41","C42","C43","C44","C45","C46","C47","C48","C49","C50","C51","C52"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct oral bioavailability measurement for the query molecule.",
    "No matched oral versus IV AUC data for the query molecule.",
    "No query-specific formulation, dose, species, or prandial-state data.",
    "L3 records provide only relative AUC/Cmax ratios, tmax, or unrelated steroid exposure; no absolute F for the query or a close quaternary analog.",
    "Potential active transport or efflux of the quaternary ammonium is not characterized in the supplied records.",
    "The reported neutral fraction (0.97) is inconsistent with the explicit quaternary ammonium charge, indicating a possible tool limitation; ionization behavior at physiological pH is uncertain."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "Predicted low: the query's permanent quaternary ammonium charge and phenolic morphinan scaffold align with multiple transferable low-F contexts (UK-224,671, estradiol, MK-458, rotigotine, catechins), all below 20%; L2 records reinforce this direction, and L3 oral exposure records are not applicable. Confidence remains moderate due to lack of direct query measurement."
}

